    <section class="msc-learn-key-terms" aria-labelledby="MscGuide012Terms"><h2 id="MscGuide012Terms">Key Terms</h2><dl><div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Transaction</dt><dd>A data structure that spends existing UTXOs and creates new outputs.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>UTXO</dt><dd>An unspent transaction output that can be used as an input in a later transaction.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Address</dt><dd>A destination representation used by wallets to construct a Bitcoin locking script.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Wallet</dt><dd>Software or hardware that manages keys, constructs transactions, and helps users interact with Bitcoin.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Coin control</dt><dd>Wallet functionality that lets a user choose which UTXOs fund a transaction.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Node</dt><dd>Bitcoin software that communicates with peers and may validate, relay, store, or serve network data.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Full node</dt><dd>Software that independently verifies Bitcoin blocks and transactions against consensus rules.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Transaction relay</dt><dd>The peer-to-peer propagation of transactions between nodes under local policy rules.</dd></div></dl></section>
